## ApacheCon Europe 2000 Special Events

Here is a list of the special features, events, and activities available at the
conference:

### Features

### O'Reilly Network Media Pavilion

Browse the Media Pavilion and pick up free copies of the latest industry
trade publications.

### Sun Microsystems' Internet Pavilion

Visit Sun's Internet Pavilion and surf the Web, pick up or send mail,
or just relax and mingle in the lounge.

### Covalent Booth in the Exhibition Area

Visit the Covalent Technologies booth in the Exhibition to sign
up for free Douglas Adams book give-aways!

### MyComponents.Com 'Best Web App Challenge'

***Get Your Web Application Funded!*** -- Enter the open source
Best Web App Challenge at
<URL:[[]http://www.mycomponents.com/](http://www.mycomponents.com/)>. The top four (4) winners
will have their projects funded for development on SourceXchange. That's
US$50,000 worth of prizes with US$47,500 toward software development
sponsored by MyComponents.com and US$2,500 in cool prizes for
outstanding proposals. Winners will be announced at ApacheCon Europe
2000.

The Web application has to be a Java-based EJB or JavaBeans running on
the open source architecture composed of the jboss EJB server and the
following Apache projects: Jetspeed, Turbine, and Tomcat. All sponsored
applications will be developed under the Apache licence. Check out the
RFP posted on SourceXchange at
<URL:[[]http://www.sourcexchange.com/](http://www.sourcexchange.com/)> for further details.

### Activities and Events

### Monday, 23 October 2000

**13h00-17h00 Sun Microsystems Technical Briefing**
Join the technologists from Sun's Java™ platform, Java development
tool, and MXL development teams as they present technology updates and
advanced topics covering application of technologies being developed
at Sun under community and open processes.
**20h30-23h30 Join the ASF at ApacheCon Europe for a night at
THE ROCK**
We invite you to a free, fun-filled social -- the IBM WebSphere
"LongevIT Spa," sponsored by IBM WebSphere.

Join us on Monday, October 23rd at:

THE ROCK

Hungerford House

Victoria Embankment

London

Round trip transportation from Olympia Centre will be provided.

**To register, visit
<URL:[[]http://www.ibm.com/websphere/spa/register3](http://www.ibm.com/websphere/spa/register3)>.
Registration is REQUIRED!**

Indulge yourself. Alleviate the stress generated from impossible turnaround
times and the pressure of integrating the latest software program with your
existing system. Have a tension-releasing head, neck and shoulder massage.
Take a virtual vacation. Refresh your software knowledge with access to IBM
WebSphere Lab, dedicated to providing you with the resources that will help
you to deliver, grow and differentiate your e-business. Or just kick back
and challenge someone to a game at a Dreamstation... It's your night. Don't
miss it!!

Space is limited, so act now and
[[]register](http://www.ibm.com/websphere/spa/register3)
or forever wonder how true peace of mind feels.

### Tuesday, 24 October 2000

**Coffee Breaks sponsored by Covalent Technologies**
Pick up your free coffee mugs!
**13h00-15h00 Oracle Developer Day**
**20h00-21h00 Reception sponsored by Covalent Technologies**
All are welcome onto the Exhibit Floor for cocktails and *hors
d'oeuvres*. Meet and mingle with fellow Apache enthusiasts and
ASF members! *Don't miss the Douglas Adams book signing!*

### Wednesday, 25 October 2000

**13h00-14h00 Wrox Press Book Signing**
Peter Wainwright, author of Professional Apache

